    "show_share": true,
    "description": "One of Abraham Mwifa's most memorable moments occurred during his elective at Aga Khan Hospital, where he was part of a team managing a critically ill patient with Acute Myocardial Infarction (AMI). \"It was a defining moment, one that reminded me exactly why I chose nursing,\" recalls the recent graduate of the Post RN-BScN programme. \"Seeing the power of interdisciplinary teamwork and realizing that I had something valuable to contribute reinforced my passion for improving cardiac care. It was humbling and inspiring at the same time.\"",
